The V3 ("KTQ", tentative name) quantizer pipeline for EXL3 trellis codes. It drives, and ports code from, the
following works:

- exllamav3 (https://github.com/turboderp-org/exllamav3), Copyright (c) 2025 Turboderp, MIT License (full text in
  LICENSES/exllamav3-MIT.txt). The EXL3 format, trellis codes, LDLQ quantiser and scale refit. This pipeline calls a
  patched fork of it (patch series in rad-exl3-mix quantize/exl3-patches/, upstream a3bfbfd0 + 0001-0007).
- rad-exl3-mix (Hero422, Apache-2.0): quantize/ourq.py (driver), proxy2b/exp/d1108/blend.py (H_in blend),
  v3/yaqa/hconv/mkhalf.py (block-normalized H_out), proxy2b/exp/w02-fixedscale/fsutil.py and v3/yaqa/swj27/ (swj),
  proxy2b/exp/w07-denoise/mkdenoise.py (writers' asymmetric target). Ported with bit-identity checks (PORTING.md).
- QTIP / YAQA (Cornell RelaxML; arXiv 2406.11235, 2505.22988): trellis-coded quantisation and the Kronecker output
  Hessian that the optional H_out stage uses.
